WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.380
Super Pitfall!

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:06.620
Join Pitfall Harry as he searches a vast subterranean cave dwelling high in the Andes.

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:29.240
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:30.300
I'm Mike.

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:31.700
I'm Sam. I'm Sean.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:33.800
And I'm Joe. What is up, guys?

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:35.860
It's Friday.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:37.960
It is. It is, yes.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:39.500
Oh, yes. It's always Friday.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:42.700
Friday in the appropriate year of the Roman calendar.

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:44.500
That's my favorite year.

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:46.760
Yeah. It's the day you're listening to this.

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:49.180
Yes, exactly. And that's the best day of all.

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:54.620
It is. We always like our listeners listening on the correct day that they choose to listen to.

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:58.120
In the present. So far, nobody has complained about listening to this in the past or the future.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:06.220
And so today we're going to talk about Super Pitfall, but I feel like we can't really talk about Super Pitfall before we talk about the non-Super Rise version of it.

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:07.540
You know, like the normal version.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:08.360
They're going to say Pong.

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:11.400
Yeah. Pong is like the normal version of all video games.

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:16.020
Yeah. Like, you know, it's like, oh, can you give me the normal version of Mario Brothers?

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:17.340
That's just Pong. Pong.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:21.800
Yep. So Pitfall came out on the Atari 2600.

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:24.720
It's pretty much considered the first platformer.

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:26.940
And also it's like an action adventure game, too.

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:28.640
So it's got two things going for it.

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:32.740
And I played it just before we did the podcast and everything like that.

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:34.740
And I think it's still fun and still holds up.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:37.080
We don't have to go like into the history and everything like that.

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:40.020
But can I just get some general feelings about the first entry, Pitfall?

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:44.040
So I played it a little bit going into this game and I thought it was fun.

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:47.240
I'd seen it so much in, you know, pop culture and stuff.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:52.500
And the little when he's swinging from the rope, it just cracked me up.

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:53.860
It's still such a good sound, too.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:54.940
Yeah. It still holds up.

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:56.500
That's supposed to be his voice.

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:58.860
It's yeah, it's like the I didn't realize that either.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:01:59.900
It's like a track.

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:03.080
But now that you say he's like, oh, yeah, I thought it was like a Tarzan.

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:04.240
Yeah, like a Tarzan kind of deal.

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:08.280
I never read that. I never did either until I did it because I heard that noise before.

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:11.680
But once I was swinging from the rope, I was like, oh, I get it now.

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:18.900
I died a lot when I was playing and I wasn't very good, but it was still I don't know.

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:21.380
It was still charming and the controls were pretty tight.

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:24.660
And, you know, it's simple, but it's good.

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:32.720
Yeah, I think I mistook the original Pitfall with the original Prince of Persia in my headcanon,

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:39.740
because I was expecting like something a little bit closer to Fidelity when I played it.

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:46.460
But no, I mean, I remembered that from when I was playing on really old systems in my childhood.

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:49.760
But, you know, it's been it's been like two decades.

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:53.820
So I've never really had any experience with this game before,

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:57.660
but I'm glad you said that about Prince of Persia, because that's the first thing that I thought of when I was playing it.

00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:04.660
It obviously didn't look like it, but just, yeah, you go from screen to screen and there's like a different little obstacle that you need to take on in each screen.

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:05.780
I thought I thought that was cool.

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:07.440
I think I would have enjoyed it.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.100
Admittedly, I didn't get to actually play this one.

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:10.540
I just watched a video of it, but it looked fun.

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:12.460
Yeah, I definitely think I think to play it.

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:18.840
I think everybody who likes video games should play this game because it's simple enough that there's no entry and you can go play it on the Internet.

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:20.580
It's it's available in a browser.

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:21.660
You might need Java.

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:23.420
Not sure about that. Ooh, Java.

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:26.440
Yeah, Java's on the way out, but not the coffee.

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:28.960
And I will kind of call my coffee Java from time to time.

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:30.860
I think I get that from the road.

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:32.720
I've never met anyone. Would you say a cup of Joe?

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:35.460
Cup of Joe? Yeah, I like cup of Joe as well.

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:37.500
I don't know why Dunkin Donuts has like a...

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:39.260
A box of Joe? Yeah, no, yeah, yeah.

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:41.920
Like they almost have like a copyright on that now.

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:43.860
Like you can't say it without people thinking about Dunkin.

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:46.620
That's my name. Sorry.

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:48.020
Welcome to the club.

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:52.160
Take a second. I've got something in my eye.

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:59.860
Fuck. There's a seltzer.

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:01.780
I gotta like pour the seltzer in my eye.

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:06.740
There's an SCP which produces a liquid...

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:09.720
It's a coffee machine that makes a liquid version of anything.

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:11.500
One of them...

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:13.780
One time someone asked it for a cup of Joe.

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:16.780
And the guy in the room named Joe started feeling sick.

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:19.660
Because he was dispensing his innards.

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:21.840
Yeah, that sucks. That's a cool SCP.

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:23.000
I know that one. Yeah.

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:25.160
Cool. Um...

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:26.560
Here we go. We're gonna start with development.

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:30.100
Okay? And I think that's enough about Pitfall.

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:31.660
Now we're gonna make things super.

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:33.680
We're gonna talk about...

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:34.940
I prefer you wouldn't.

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:38.340
Yeah, yeah. I was saying you don't look very amused over there on the other end of the table, Sean.

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:39.780
But we have to talk about it.

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:41.920
It is today... It is the game of the week.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:43.880
And we'll start with the development.

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:47.440
So this game was made by Micronics and published by Activision.

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:50.380
Activision's kind of like all over the place with us recently.

00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:53.180
But I think I'm also confusing them with Acclaim.

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:54.820
Like, because they both start with...

00:04:54.820 --> 00:04:56.500
Hey, I just... The games blend together for me.

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:57.480
And they're both just publishers.

00:04:57.720 --> 00:05:01.680
I think that the true red flag here is Micronics.

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:06.160
Okay. Because they don't really have a solid track record with us either.

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:11.840
Mm-hmm. Uh, I don't quite remember the game that I'm thinking of.

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:13.240
But it was very bad. But the name...

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:18.580
Just the fact that the name is sticking with you is also not a great sign of, like, things to come.

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:22.320
And also, Pitfall was made by a guy named David Crane.

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:25.600
And he has nothing to do with Super Pitfall.

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:30.380
So it's just kind of like Activision cashing in on the Pitfall name and saying,

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:31.980
Hey, we can do this.

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:33.700
Let's do this. So they do.

00:05:34.460 --> 00:05:36.940
And what do they really take from Pitfall?

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:38.800
You can fall? You can jump?

00:05:39.260 --> 00:05:43.720
Well, also, like, in Pitfall, you were searching for 20 treasures.

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:46.260
And in this one, you're searching for, like, three different things.

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:54.280
So the idea of still, like, searching for treasure counts for something, even if treasure is now your niece and your pet.

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:55.260
Pet lion. Yeah.

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:56.920
And all those other things.

00:05:57.340 --> 00:06:01.940
Also, Sean, you're thinking of both 1942 and elevator action.

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:04.840
There it is. But, Ghost and Goblins.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:10.160
So, I mean, but that groundwork was laid out in the arcade version.

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:11.320
And the arcade version is better.

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:12.780
So, I think, like, even though...

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:14.920
Those were not Micronics in the arcade.

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:16.180
No, the arcade was Capcom.

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:19.200
Yeah. There we go. And also, like, some other things I'm noticing now.

00:06:19.280 --> 00:06:20.960
Ikari Warriors, they also did.

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:22.080
Tiger Heli.

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:25.500
So, things were made by Micronics around 87.

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:26.640
They're all over the place.

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:30.040
Let's do some first impressions for Super Pitfall.

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:36.840
Sean? I feel like with Super Pitfall, it was, like, sort of stepping into somebody's, like, chewed-up gum.

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:41.620
Because it looks like it was good in its original form.

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:45.760
And now it's just this mass of just, like, icky garbage.

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:50.660
And I'm sort of coloring the rest of my reaction to this game.

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:54.500
But I think that the fact that it's an open world is great.

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:58.100
As far as an open world game can be at this level.

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:00.300
It's just filled with garbage.

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:03.280
Garbage enemies. Garbage platforming.

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:04.240
The jump is bad.

00:07:05.380 --> 00:07:07.040
And this is my first impression.

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:10.040
Because this is just thrown at you in the first 20 seconds.

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:14.760
All of these terrible mechanics are just thrust upon you.

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:15.740
And he shoots a gun.

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:17.600
That doesn't hit anything. Alright.

00:07:17.820 --> 00:07:18.800
Joe? Yeah.

00:07:18.900 --> 00:07:23.220
My first impression was definitely a lot about the controls kind of not feeling great.

00:07:23.260 --> 00:07:27.240
And also about, like, the lack of direction.

00:07:27.240 --> 00:07:29.140
Like, I wasn't really sure what I'm supposed to be doing.

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:30.220
Am I supposed to get that?

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:33.400
Am I supposed to get the gold? Like, there's a bunch of little things that I just feel like...

00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:34.260
Did you read the manual?

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:35.340
I read the manual.

00:07:35.460 --> 00:07:36.320
The gold gives you points.

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:39.540
But, I mean, I just felt like, after a while, I was just, like, lost.

00:07:39.820 --> 00:07:41.220
And I was just, you know, it wasn't...

00:07:41.220 --> 00:07:43.180
I don't know. It didn't...

00:07:44.920 --> 00:07:50.000
The gameplay did not make up for the fact that I'm wandering around this world I don't want to want.

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:51.740
Like, there was no fun to wandering around.

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:55.940
Like, if you're lost in a game like that, like, think of Metroid.

00:07:55.940 --> 00:07:59.120
You can get lost in that, but you're having fun searching.

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:01.060
And this, I was not having fun off the bat.

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:11.700
Yes. And my first impression is discovered right away when the first ladder in the game is actually just a spike trap with, like, a bat.

00:08:11.940 --> 00:08:13.840
Like, it's just a pit of death.

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:15.500
Like, the ladder just ends.

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:17.440
You can't see what's about to happen.

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:21.040
But when you drop down from the ladder, you fall into a pit and die.

00:08:21.220 --> 00:08:22.120
And I was like...

00:08:22.120 --> 00:08:23.400
What kind of pitfall? Yeah.

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:24.680
On the one hand, like, that's...

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:28.900
Well, that's pretty realistic to what would probably happen in a real cave if you followed ladders around.

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:32.460
But on the other hand, I don't need that in a video game.

00:08:32.460 --> 00:08:38.880
And I also wish that that information was communicated better on a screen of, like, being able to see what you're going to fall down to.

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:41.740
This is going to be a huge problem throughout the rest of the game.

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:46.780
But I just think it's so weird that in the very first thing you're introduced to is don't trust ladders.

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:49.060
When climbing ladders is most of the game.

00:08:49.160 --> 00:08:51.620
It is good advice, though, for this game.

00:08:51.840 --> 00:09:00.580
I get the feeling that they were trying to do the tutorial like Mario does in the first few seconds of where it's like, oh, this is what you need to do.

00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:04.000
But instead, it kind of just comes off as, like, this game's going to suck.

00:09:04.880 --> 00:09:05.940
Don't try anything.

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:07.020
Don't try anything but funny.

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:09.820
It comes off as, like, you can't trust what you're seeing.

00:09:09.820 --> 00:09:14.300
And, like, there's not really going to be a clue to what you're supposed to, like, what you can climb down and what you can't.

00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:15.340
You can't trust what you see.

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:16.760
You can't trust what you do.

00:09:16.940 --> 00:09:19.420
Right. You know, it's, you can't really trust this game.

00:09:19.420 --> 00:09:21.140
And that goes straight through to the end of the game.

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:22.460
You can't trust what's happening.

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:24.280
Because, like, we'll get into that later, I'm sure.

00:09:25.020 --> 00:09:28.320
All right. So, as I do, I like to read the manual first.

00:09:28.940 --> 00:09:33.180
So, while I was looking up the manual, this is, like, before first impressions.

00:09:33.480 --> 00:09:34.740
These are, like, pre-impressions.

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:37.920
I looked up Super Pitfall.

00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:42.840
And the first thing, one of the first things that comes up is map.

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:45.280
Or, like, route. And so I'm thinking, okay, cool.

00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:50.260
This is, this is interesting that there's, you know, a specific way you have to go through.

00:09:50.380 --> 00:09:54.940
So before I even read the manual, I knew that it was some kind of open world-ish kind of game.

00:09:54.940 --> 00:10:03.440
And then I read the beginning of the manual, which said that there are over 270 different screens in this game.

00:10:03.440 --> 00:10:06.120
And that's when the red flags started to come up.

00:10:06.340 --> 00:10:11.080
Because with a game with that many screens, they can't all be good.

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:16.260
You know, it's got to be just a bunch of useless stuff.

00:10:17.080 --> 00:10:20.920
And then my suspicions were pretty much confirmed when I got in.

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:27.820
But I think the most jarring thing off the bat is that, I don't know, 15-second song that repeats.

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:30.440
Not the best song either.

00:10:30.660 --> 00:10:33.420
Like, 15-second songs can be okay certain times.

00:10:33.620 --> 00:10:34.920
Not when they're not clutch.

00:10:36.460 --> 00:10:46.540
Besides that, one positive thing that I liked was that, depending on how quickly you press the A button, your character jumps different heights.

00:10:46.720 --> 00:10:50.520
Which I thought was, you know, they did it in, you know, Super Mario Bros.

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:59.040
But for a game that looked and felt this bad, I thought that that was kind of a cool thing right off the bat.

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:03.600
That you can kind of do little jumps if you want to not hit your head on something.

00:11:03.860 --> 00:11:07.780
Sure. But whoever programmed this game did not think it through.

00:11:07.880 --> 00:11:12.420
Because I think the controls are some of the poorest that we've played other than wrestling games.

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:14.180
It's real bad. That's the one silver lining.

00:11:14.320 --> 00:11:15.680
It's like, oh, I can control my jump height.

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:21.560
Right. That was it. And so, since you mentioned the manual, we might as well go into a little Tales from the Manual section.

00:11:21.560 --> 00:11:24.820
Because I have two points of information that I'd like to talk about.

00:11:25.380 --> 00:11:27.420
The first has nothing to do with the manual.

00:11:27.440 --> 00:11:30.440
So, I really got to think of a better name for this Tales from the Manual section.

00:11:31.220 --> 00:11:32.500
Tales from the Marketing. Yeah.

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:33.800
Tales from Marketing.

00:11:33.800 --> 00:11:38.840
Well, Super Pitfall is actually a loose remake of Pitfall 2 Lost Caverns.

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:42.600
And from what I can tell, it must have been a very loose remake.

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:44.880
Maybe, like, only the plot was carried over.

00:11:45.080 --> 00:11:51.040
Because Pitfall 2 The Lost Caverns seems like a decently playable game that Pitfall fans probably liked.

00:11:51.220 --> 00:11:53.460
It was sort of like Pitfall in some way?

00:11:53.460 --> 00:11:59.340
In some ways, but also, like, the idea that you're exploring caves and stuff this time instead of, like, a jungle.

00:11:59.700 --> 00:12:01.480
Okay. Pitfall 1 is all, like, in a jungle.

00:12:02.340 --> 00:12:09.100
And then, in the manual for Super Pitfall, there's a tips and tricks section, you know, towards, like, the end of it.

00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:16.200
And it tells you, like, a bunch of things that, of pieces of advice that you might need to play the game and to get through the game properly.

00:12:16.320 --> 00:12:18.200
And we've seen this before in other manuals.

00:12:18.200 --> 00:12:21.840
Sometimes it gives you, like, a riddle or, like, a vague hint.

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:27.040
Or there's that other one about the Medusa in Starforce that was, like, it's worth a million points.

00:12:27.040 --> 00:12:27.840
Can you find it?

00:12:28.320 --> 00:12:33.860
Well, in Super Pitfall, the manual just tells you that the best way to get through the cave is to explore it.

00:12:35.640 --> 00:12:40.320
That's not even, like, that would make sense if it was in the objective or in, like, the beginning of the manual.

00:12:40.520 --> 00:12:44.220
But in the tips and tricks section, it's the only thing you can do.

00:12:44.220 --> 00:12:51.160
Didn't we just have another game like that where it's directions on how to play were just, like, beat the game?

00:12:51.220 --> 00:12:57.340
No, it was just over description of, like, pressing A button will do what the A button does.

00:12:57.800 --> 00:13:01.820
Whereas, yeah, the best way to explore the cave is to explore it.

00:13:02.220 --> 00:13:03.380
And it's like, thanks.

00:13:03.620 --> 00:13:05.320
Yeah. And then they do it again.

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:08.900
But there's only one way to play the game, right?

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:10.400
Like, you would have to explore the cave.

00:13:10.540 --> 00:13:13.980
It's literally the only, it's, no one ever got confused about that.

00:13:14.220 --> 00:13:16.540
No one started the game, dropped it in the cave, and said, I shouldn't be here.

00:13:16.700 --> 00:13:18.760
And, like, put down the console and control it.

00:13:18.860 --> 00:13:21.400
But then right after that, they have tried to discover the shortest route.

00:13:21.620 --> 00:13:24.220
You may just uncover an unexpected shortcut in the process.

00:13:24.940 --> 00:13:28.060
So, by searching for the shortest route, you may find the shortest route.

00:13:29.360 --> 00:13:31.180
Or an even shorter route than you were expecting.

00:13:31.520 --> 00:13:37.100
Yeah. Right. I was always expecting very long routes because, you know, and we'll get into this in the gameplay section,

00:13:37.100 --> 00:13:41.960
but navigating your way through this cave is kind of like, if you fall deep enough into the cave,

00:13:41.960 --> 00:13:43.440
you're kind of stuck there for a while.

00:13:43.700 --> 00:13:46.840
Like, you know, you're not about to just be like, oh, it'll just be like, you know,

00:13:46.920 --> 00:13:48.400
a couple seconds before I'm back up at the top.

00:13:48.780 --> 00:13:49.600
No, you're down there.

00:13:49.620 --> 00:13:53.940
Yeah, yeah. If you fall off of, like, one level, but there just happens to be the right kind of,

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:58.080
or the wrong kind of area below you, you'll just fall for, like, 40 minutes.

00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:01.100
You'll fall for 40 minutes, and then there's nothing you can do about it.

00:14:01.100 --> 00:14:03.240
You're passing things that it looks like you can land on.

00:14:03.300 --> 00:14:04.140
You can't.

00:14:04.140 --> 00:14:06.940
You can't move your player, correct?

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:12.680
Right. You have a certain amount of jump control, but that's only once you've hit the top of your arc.

00:14:12.960 --> 00:14:13.800
Not once you, like, fall.

00:14:13.800 --> 00:14:17.680
No, yeah, but once you're falling, you can't, like, will yourself a certain way.

00:14:17.760 --> 00:14:22.100
Like, in Super Mario Bros., when you fall from any height, you can still control Mario's momentum.

00:14:22.560 --> 00:14:23.780
Not so in Super Pitfall.

00:14:23.860 --> 00:14:26.420
You are locked to a free fall, straight down.

00:14:26.620 --> 00:14:28.920
Like, put the controller down, have a bathroom break.

00:14:29.240 --> 00:14:30.740
You're going to be falling for a while.

00:14:31.280 --> 00:14:33.320
So, real fast, I'll do the objective here.

00:14:33.320 --> 00:14:41.240
In Super Pitfall, you have to locate a diamond, your niece, and your pet quickclaw, who is a lion, as Sam mentioned earlier.

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:45.420
And you do this through a vast set of cave, of one cave.

00:14:45.580 --> 00:14:46.900
I was going to say caves. Vast set of cave.

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:51.800
Honestly, you know, with the way these translations work out sometimes, that might have been in the game.

00:14:51.900 --> 00:14:54.280
Yeah. You're given no map.

00:14:54.400 --> 00:14:56.080
You must explore the cave.

00:14:56.340 --> 00:14:58.900
And there's zero guidance to find any of those things.

00:14:59.060 --> 00:15:04.000
So, if you want to find the diamond, the niece, your pet quickclaw, the manual wasn't telling you anything.

00:15:04.140 --> 00:15:05.800
But the game isn't also telling you anything either.

00:15:06.020 --> 00:15:10.100
There's no character in the game who says, like, hey, I think your niece is this way.

00:15:10.260 --> 00:15:13.300
Or, like, a sign with your niece or something like that.

00:15:13.400 --> 00:15:14.440
Like, anything that would help you.

00:15:14.440 --> 00:15:17.660
You just have to kind of explore the cave and figure out where those things are.

00:15:17.900 --> 00:15:21.560
You're limited to jumping, climbing ladders, and shooting a gun.

00:15:21.980 --> 00:15:23.520
One hit and you're dead.

00:15:23.920 --> 00:15:26.820
Similar games we've played are Spelunker and Metroid.

00:15:27.080 --> 00:15:29.140
I think that's my objective setup.

00:15:29.140 --> 00:15:35.140
So, now that everybody understands the game that we're talking about, I'm sure they're picturing it vividly in their heads, we can talk gameplay.

00:15:35.140 --> 00:15:35.940
Who wants to start?

00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:37.400
I'll start real quick.

00:15:37.760 --> 00:15:43.080
While you may be vividly imagining what the game is like, it's very much not that.

00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:50.300
Because if you are thinking, like, okay, you go around, you search for keys, and then they'll unlock doors.

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:53.500
Like, yeah, there are keys and there are doors, but you can't see the keys.

00:15:53.880 --> 00:15:55.760
And you really can't see the doors.

00:15:56.440 --> 00:16:00.360
And you also don't really see much of anything.

00:16:00.440 --> 00:16:07.500
Because everything that you're trying to find does not have a sprite until you jump and get it.

00:16:07.580 --> 00:16:09.540
Like, you won't even get it just walking around.

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:12.140
They're hidden so poorly.

00:16:12.140 --> 00:16:14.780
Like, it's not even a fun experience, I think.

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:17.240
I feel like maybe some people did, but...

00:16:17.240 --> 00:16:19.100
It's not because here's why also.

00:16:19.420 --> 00:16:22.220
Like, so you said with enemies just kind of pop in, right?

00:16:22.340 --> 00:16:26.300
Like, all of a sudden a frog is like mid-jump, even though you didn't see him a second ago.

00:16:26.440 --> 00:16:29.060
And then you just take one step back and he despawns, right?

00:16:29.060 --> 00:16:31.180
It's like, oh, great job, programmers.

00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:35.160
Like, I'll just glitch my way through the cave that I'm clearly hallucinating.

00:17:03.740 --> 00:17:05.140
It's hallucinating.

00:17:05.140 --> 00:17:10.560
And just, like, perfectly sync up over and over and over again on loop so that you can't get through anything.

00:17:10.760 --> 00:17:18.900
And so in that situation, you have to kind of, like, leave that area and come back and hope that the waterfall, like, recesses itself properly.

00:17:19.160 --> 00:17:22.220
Yeah. And so, like, good job there, too.

00:17:22.380 --> 00:17:25.480
I think we can talk a lot about, like, the glitches and errors of this game, though.

00:17:25.700 --> 00:17:27.160
Because even just...

00:17:27.700 --> 00:17:28.840
Even when it's performing...

00:17:28.840 --> 00:17:31.440
Even when it's acting as it should, it performs terribly.

00:17:31.740 --> 00:17:34.920
Right. Nothing about this game's controls are satisfying.

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:37.300
Because even shooting your gun, right?

00:17:37.500 --> 00:17:40.600
Like, you would expect, like, okay, I shoot the gun.

00:17:40.760 --> 00:17:42.000
The bullet comes out.

00:17:42.480 --> 00:17:43.460
There's the spider.

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:46.120
And then it just goes right past the spider.

00:17:46.280 --> 00:17:49.880
It's like... Yeah. And then I realized, oh, no, that's just something that can never be killed.

00:17:50.180 --> 00:17:51.060
Yeah, you can kill spiders.

00:17:51.100 --> 00:17:54.040
You're supposed to... I don't know if it works on spiders or not, but you're supposed to, like...

00:17:54.040 --> 00:17:58.420
There's little dips that have, like, a small ladder or a small area you can, like, go in.

00:17:58.500 --> 00:18:03.260
And if you go in there, jump up a little bit and shoot, the bullet will be at the right level to hit those lower things.

00:18:04.260 --> 00:18:06.020
Those situations are so rare.

00:18:06.240 --> 00:18:08.480
But at that point, you're better off just jumping over these.

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:09.840
Yeah, really. They're also harmless.

00:18:10.240 --> 00:18:11.520
It's weird, because you can crouch.

00:18:12.060 --> 00:18:14.320
And I thought maybe that's why you would tell you to do that.

00:18:14.340 --> 00:18:15.820
What does that do? It doesn't do anything.

00:18:15.820 --> 00:18:19.400
Because your hitbox, even when you're standing, doesn't affect your head.

00:18:19.600 --> 00:18:23.620
Yeah. Well, I guess there's, like, the bats that, like, fly in that little swoopy pattern.

00:18:23.620 --> 00:18:24.800
The hitbox is the same.

00:18:24.900 --> 00:18:26.380
Yeah? The hitbox is the same.

00:18:26.560 --> 00:18:28.560
Those bats really angered me.

00:18:28.700 --> 00:18:31.560
So I think, like, one thing, though, is, like, we're talking about frogs.

00:18:31.620 --> 00:18:32.820
We're talking about spiders.

00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:34.180
We're talking about bats.

00:18:34.440 --> 00:18:36.500
The cave's got a variety of enemies.

00:18:36.720 --> 00:18:39.080
The problem is that there's no way to handle these enemies.

00:18:39.340 --> 00:18:41.980
Yeah. The only thing you can do is shoot a frog in the face.

00:18:42.120 --> 00:18:43.000
If it's a midjump.

00:18:43.000 --> 00:18:44.660
Oh, and the scorpions, too.

00:18:44.720 --> 00:18:47.500
Those things got me. Yeah, and they charge at you, too.

00:18:47.740 --> 00:18:50.620
They run at you. Yeah, so they give you, like, a nice variety of enemies.

00:18:50.640 --> 00:18:56.600
But the problem is that the way that the game controls itself, you can't really handle any of these enemies properly.

00:18:56.600 --> 00:18:59.240
Maybe if it were less crowded.

00:18:59.260 --> 00:19:00.960
It's a very crowded cave.

00:19:01.180 --> 00:19:08.880
And I sometimes will just have to avoid just going anywhere where there's any kind of resistance.

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:11.840
Because I just die so often.

00:19:12.220 --> 00:19:14.460
And you only get three tries.

00:19:14.620 --> 00:19:16.240
So you don't really want to risk it.

00:19:16.360 --> 00:19:22.000
Like, the design of the game actually punishes you for exploring in some ways.

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:36.620
Yeah. Well, I think the biggest thing that punishes you for exploring at all, and, you know, to Pitfall's, like, you know, credit, this is one of the things that the original game had going for it was, like, the traps and the, you know, like, avoid the alligators when their mouths are open.

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:39.540
Or, you know, like, don't fall into the pits, you know?

00:19:39.720 --> 00:19:41.580
Like, that makes sense. It kind of telegraphs that stuff to you.

00:19:41.580 --> 00:19:42.560
Right, it telegraphs that stuff to you.

00:19:42.560 --> 00:19:53.920
In this game, it's filled with different kinds of traps, but none of them you're prepared for because they're a screen over that you fall into, or they're as you're coming up to them, like, a new enemy is there.

00:19:53.920 --> 00:19:57.680
The ceiling will just spontaneously fall with no, like, when you're under it.

00:19:57.880 --> 00:20:05.700
Yeah. All of a sudden, a, you know, there's a part where the top of the ceiling of the cave kind of collapses onto you.

00:20:05.700 --> 00:20:13.300
So, and, like, cool idea, you know, I think, like, also that would kill anybody and should realistically block the path back the other way.

00:20:13.880 --> 00:20:21.060
But if you want to do it in the game, I'm fine with that, but also it's just, it was never communicated to that point, so you're absolutely going to die the first time it happens.

00:20:21.480 --> 00:20:22.680
And is it only the one spot?

00:20:22.800 --> 00:20:24.460
I feel like maybe I just, like, backtracked.

00:20:24.460 --> 00:20:27.540
I feel like it just happens at some spots, and there's no way of knowing what's going to happen.

00:20:27.620 --> 00:20:30.160
It's not really a puzzle, it's just, you're going to die.

00:20:30.680 --> 00:20:35.720
That's it. I don't think they're random, but I definitely think it happens, like, in multiple places throughout the game.

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:39.580
I think the game exposes you to a lot early on in terms of exploration.

00:20:39.740 --> 00:20:48.900
Like, you can go a bunch of different ways and experience a bunch of different things, but after a while, you've kind of seen the cave.

00:20:49.100 --> 00:20:54.260
Yeah. And now you're just kind of like, where is any of the things I need to find, right?

00:20:54.260 --> 00:20:58.780
Like, how did people do on finding the diamond, the niece, or the pet?

00:20:58.960 --> 00:20:59.980
I found the diamond.

00:20:59.980 --> 00:21:01.240
And that's it.

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:02.280
I didn't find anything.

00:21:03.800 --> 00:21:11.720
Also, I just wanted to note that in the manual, even when you find Rhonda, it says that she's been turned to stone,

00:21:11.720 --> 00:21:15.500
and so that you have to find a flask of medicine also.

00:21:15.780 --> 00:21:16.920
So that's not even...

00:21:16.920 --> 00:21:19.860
Yeah, but that's like, yeah, that's like the twist early on.

00:21:20.180 --> 00:21:22.100
Yeah, but it tells you that first thing in the manual also.

00:21:22.320 --> 00:21:26.180
Right, but I guess, like, you know, it's the prologue of the game.

00:21:26.340 --> 00:21:29.100
Not that anybody would stick around for longer than the prologue.

00:21:29.200 --> 00:21:30.900
Yeah. I wouldn't recommend it.

00:21:31.300 --> 00:21:33.740
So we have issues with the jump.

00:21:33.740 --> 00:21:35.080
We have issues with the gun.

00:21:35.700 --> 00:21:38.480
There's a lot of enemies, but they're too small to even hit with your gun.

00:21:39.200 --> 00:21:41.240
We didn't even talk about the limited ammunition.

00:21:41.880 --> 00:21:44.540
So in your gun, you get, I think, 12 bullets?

00:21:44.780 --> 00:21:46.880
20. 20? Who cares?

00:21:47.360 --> 00:21:51.040
Yeah. That's how I, when I ran out of bullets, I was like, all right, I just won't shoot anymore.

00:21:51.200 --> 00:21:52.480
It hasn't done anything for me.

00:21:52.480 --> 00:21:56.720
Yeah, they tried to make it like a use them carefully because these are precious and you're

00:21:56.720 --> 00:21:59.940
going to need them. And it's like, I don't think I really need them.

00:22:00.160 --> 00:22:03.360
Like, I'll just, honestly, I'll just, with the frogs, I'll just go the other way.

00:22:04.600 --> 00:22:07.580
You know, like, honestly, in this cave, I'm thinking about how do I get back up to where

00:22:07.580 --> 00:22:08.860
I came from and just leave?

00:22:09.140 --> 00:22:11.400
Yeah. And it's not like the bullets work, also.

00:22:11.660 --> 00:22:15.620
I feel like the hitboxes were so bad on the enemies that I would have to shoot the bat

00:22:15.620 --> 00:22:17.620
three times before we'd even get hit.

00:22:17.840 --> 00:22:20.560
Yeah, and then you're down to 17 and good luck finding more ammo.

00:22:20.660 --> 00:22:21.840
There is more ammo, but...

00:22:21.840 --> 00:22:25.160
It's hidden the same way that the keys are hidden, where you don't really see it until

00:22:25.160 --> 00:22:27.240
you jump up and accidentally touch it.

00:22:27.400 --> 00:22:30.600
Right. And that's even how the secret warps are dealt with in this game.

00:22:31.180 --> 00:22:33.040
Did we mention there's secret warps?

00:22:33.280 --> 00:22:35.300
Yeah, there's secret warps to better manage your trip.

00:22:35.900 --> 00:22:37.540
Secret, is that what they say in the mail?

00:22:37.560 --> 00:22:42.180
I don't know. Okay. But secret warps in this game work a little differently, though, because sometimes secret

00:22:42.180 --> 00:22:47.680
warps are, like, required to get back to other parts of the cave that you maybe fell from

00:22:47.680 --> 00:22:49.540
or that you want to get back to.

00:22:50.240 --> 00:22:51.900
That doesn't seem like that should be the case.

00:22:52.000 --> 00:22:55.080
It should be that any way to get to this cave should be completely explorable.

00:22:55.540 --> 00:22:59.660
There should never be, like, a drop-off point unless it was going to act like a Metroidvania

00:22:59.660 --> 00:23:04.780
where it's like, once you drop off, you can only get back to the top with the new item.

00:23:05.040 --> 00:23:12.400
Yeah. You know? That level of design understanding is beyond the developer of this game.

00:23:12.600 --> 00:23:19.000
Yes. One of the warps is actually an enemy that you have to get hit by.

00:23:19.160 --> 00:23:20.720
And what's the problem with that, Sean?

00:23:22.880 --> 00:23:27.240
The problem with that is that you have been trained from the beginning of this game to

00:23:27.240 --> 00:23:29.700
either avoid or destroy enemies.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:34.160
I mean, it would take you forever to figure that out, even by accident.

00:23:34.160 --> 00:23:37.740
Or, like, if you're intentionally doing it, you still don't know which enemy or anything.

00:23:37.880 --> 00:23:41.100
Surely the bird is colored differently or looks different.

00:23:41.100 --> 00:23:43.960
The bird looks exactly like the other birds that can kill you, Mike.

00:23:43.960 --> 00:23:45.340
No way.

00:23:45.960 --> 00:23:47.020
It is true.

00:23:47.220 --> 00:23:50.600
And I only found this out by watching a video thing later on.

00:23:50.780 --> 00:23:51.980
I can't believe that.

00:23:52.160 --> 00:23:58.160
That is the kind of stuff that when people say Nintendo hard, that's what I really think about.

00:23:58.640 --> 00:24:00.400
No, Nintendo game is designed that way.

00:24:00.400 --> 00:24:04.380
Yeah, I know, but I'm saying, like, that's the kind of bullshit I expect from these kinds of games.

00:24:04.460 --> 00:24:10.600
But this is the first, like, example I can think of where a game has, like, mandatory parts of it.

00:24:10.740 --> 00:24:15.700
Like, sometimes you will need to use that secret warp if you forgot something earlier on to get back to that area.

00:24:16.120 --> 00:24:19.080
And it's like, how would that be communicated to anybody?

00:24:19.080 --> 00:24:21.480
Were they trying to sell a guidebook later on?

00:24:21.660 --> 00:24:25.680
I don't know. That has to be something along those lines, because I know that they did exist.

00:24:25.880 --> 00:24:27.240
Like, there were strategy guides.

00:24:27.260 --> 00:24:28.780
It's not even clever.

00:24:28.780 --> 00:24:30.320
Never. Nowhere.

00:24:30.720 --> 00:24:37.480
You know, secret warps existing in an otherwise totally realistic world is, you know, mind-boggling enough.

00:24:37.620 --> 00:24:41.980
But then to think, like, oh, and one of those secret worlds would just be a bird that you jump into.

00:24:42.160 --> 00:24:44.460
It would be fun if that were, like, an Easter egg.

00:24:44.900 --> 00:24:46.080
Or maybe there was...

00:24:46.080 --> 00:24:47.160
Takes you to a treasure room.

00:24:47.280 --> 00:24:48.620
Yeah. Something like that.

00:24:48.740 --> 00:24:52.140
But if it's actually necessary, then no.

00:24:52.640 --> 00:24:57.000
No. There was a thing in The Goonies, too, that had that same thing, right?

00:24:57.100 --> 00:24:58.320
It was Hit the Woman Five Time.

00:24:58.320 --> 00:25:00.960
Yeah. Oh, yeah. And then you get an evident required item.

00:25:00.960 --> 00:25:02.460
I don't know if it was a woman, but I think it was.

00:25:02.560 --> 00:25:03.840
I think it was an old woman. It was an old lady.

00:25:03.920 --> 00:25:05.700
Yeah, an old lady, and you gotta hit her five times.

00:25:05.820 --> 00:25:12.660
All right. Whatever. And so, you know, we touched lightly on the exploration thing, I think, for the most part.

00:25:12.660 --> 00:25:13.580
I feel good about that.

00:25:13.660 --> 00:25:18.920
But can we talk about how there are no cave exploration items to be found in this game?

00:25:18.920 --> 00:25:24.520
I felt like a flashlight would have been nice, maybe some hiking gear, like, you know, a hookshot.

00:25:24.780 --> 00:25:25.660
Where were these things?

00:25:25.660 --> 00:25:26.600
So, all right.

00:25:27.040 --> 00:25:31.920
Do you, Mike, you know the trademark swinging ropes, right?

00:25:32.240 --> 00:25:34.020
Yes. So those are from Pitfall.

00:25:34.200 --> 00:25:35.700
They're also in Pitfall 2.

00:25:35.960 --> 00:25:37.220
Super Pitfall, I'm sorry.

00:25:37.420 --> 00:25:42.120
Yeah. Well, this is a loose adaptation of Pitfall 2.

00:25:42.440 --> 00:25:46.160
Did you notice that they were sort of, like, phasing in and out of existence?

00:25:46.640 --> 00:25:49.640
Everything in this game, at one point or another, will phase in and out.

00:25:49.640 --> 00:25:52.520
But no, I didn't notice this specific instance.

00:25:52.740 --> 00:25:55.980
I think that they pushed the engine.

00:25:55.980 --> 00:25:59.220
I mean, I don't even know if it's an engine that they built this game in.

00:25:59.300 --> 00:26:05.640
But they pushed the software so hard just to get the ropes to exist in some dimension.

00:26:05.640 --> 00:26:11.800
That I don't think that there would be any processing power left to create, like, a hookshot.

00:26:12.220 --> 00:26:14.620
Let alone an inventory system, too.

00:26:14.920 --> 00:26:16.600
You know? Like, I don't think so.

00:26:16.820 --> 00:26:18.400
Yeah. But it's something that I would have liked.

00:26:19.140 --> 00:26:22.060
And then, what happens when you beat the game?

00:26:23.400 --> 00:26:26.660
Joe. Well, let me break it to you here.

00:26:26.720 --> 00:26:27.760
I didn't beat the game.

00:26:27.920 --> 00:26:29.280
Okay, that's fair. Do you know?

00:26:29.280 --> 00:26:34.720
I did watch the playthrough, and I saw that at the end you get to, what, your niece that you're trying to rescue?

00:26:34.720 --> 00:26:38.400
You get her, and then that's, you're still playing the game.

00:26:38.700 --> 00:26:40.540
Yes. So you don't even get out, right?

00:26:41.100 --> 00:26:42.580
You have to go back somewhere.

00:26:43.060 --> 00:26:47.580
But, like, it didn't seem clearly indicated, even once you got there, why you've now, why it's over.

00:26:47.700 --> 00:26:49.580
I would imagine that you have to get out first.

00:26:49.860 --> 00:26:52.040
I don't know the exact clear conditions.

00:26:52.040 --> 00:26:55.920
I just know that when you clear, and we can find out the clear conditions in a minute.

00:26:55.920 --> 00:27:01.920
But once you clear the game, all you get is just offer to play in another world.

00:27:02.320 --> 00:27:03.960
Oh, yeah. That's the actual ending.

00:27:04.180 --> 00:27:10.120
Yeah. And it's just, this new world is just another game of Super Pitfall.

00:27:10.360 --> 00:27:13.240
But all of the items are switched to different locations.

00:27:13.460 --> 00:27:16.220
Which are already hidden. Like, no thanks.

00:27:16.500 --> 00:27:19.660
It was hard enough to find out the first time without any indication of anything.

00:27:19.660 --> 00:27:25.040
This is the equivalent of, like, solving a puzzle, you know, like an actual jigsaw puzzle.

00:27:25.220 --> 00:27:29.460
And then after you solve it, they give you the option to solve the same puzzle.

00:27:29.580 --> 00:27:35.160
Like, you'll complete the same picture, but they change the shape of the jigsaws inside, you know?

00:27:35.280 --> 00:27:36.300
That's not helpful.

00:27:36.300 --> 00:27:37.120
That's not interesting.

00:27:37.140 --> 00:27:41.920
It's also not another realm or another dimension or whatever they said.

00:27:42.220 --> 00:27:45.100
Right. It's just, it's just things moved, things in different places.

00:27:45.760 --> 00:27:51.080
Let me give you the description of, like, how I watched the game end.

00:27:51.260 --> 00:27:57.900
A lot of the things that I've learned about this game, I watched by, I learned by watching an AGDQ run.

00:27:58.660 --> 00:27:59.900
What is AGDQ?

00:28:00.300 --> 00:28:01.580
Awesome Games Done Quick.

00:28:01.780 --> 00:28:04.900
A little speed running marathon that's done two times a year.

00:28:05.040 --> 00:28:07.340
Yeah. You got Awesome and then you got Summer Games Done Quick.

00:28:07.500 --> 00:28:10.240
Very good. I don't know which one this was.

00:28:10.240 --> 00:28:11.160
I think it was Awesome.

00:28:12.360 --> 00:28:14.120
But it did it in seven minutes.

00:28:15.500 --> 00:28:24.900
And the way he beat the game was he got his niece and then he just died three times and ran out of his lives.

00:28:25.080 --> 00:28:28.720
And then he got to the title screen and waited for, like, the demo to run.

00:28:29.420 --> 00:28:34.520
And that pretty much works the same as whatever the other endgame, like, flag is supposed to be.

00:28:39.200 --> 00:28:47.360
And that's how the game ends, to me.

00:28:47.440 --> 00:28:51.280
I'm trying to even figure out how those are, like, accidentally connected.

00:28:51.500 --> 00:28:54.520
It's just poor, like, script programming.

00:28:54.520 --> 00:29:00.980
Yeah. And so I'm watching it now and it's kind of incredible.

00:29:00.980 --> 00:29:02.740
You do have to leave the cave.

00:29:02.920 --> 00:29:08.900
You find out that you've been in Egypt this whole time because every game takes place in Egypt at one point or another.

00:29:08.900 --> 00:29:12.380
One stage is going to casually reveal to you that there's pyramids in it.

00:29:12.500 --> 00:29:22.900
So you see the pyramids and then the game just all of a sudden just starts, like, fluttering between, like, a black strobe and the actual gameplay.

00:29:23.000 --> 00:29:27.160
And then it just comes up and says, please try another world.

00:29:28.060 --> 00:29:30.100
That sounds like you've got the wrong number.

00:29:30.520 --> 00:29:34.500
Yeah. Like, you've been playing the wrong game and they tell you once you've finished it.

00:29:34.560 --> 00:29:35.980
Like, oh, wait, this wasn't the game.

00:29:35.980 --> 00:29:37.840
That was somebody else's niece.

00:29:38.940 --> 00:29:40.880
You have to go back and find your niece.

00:29:41.080 --> 00:29:42.660
You don't recognize your own niece?

00:29:42.940 --> 00:29:45.880
That was also, like, a gumshoe problem, right?

00:29:46.280 --> 00:29:47.840
Later that same day.

00:29:48.000 --> 00:29:49.760
Yeah, later that same day she's kidnapped.

00:29:50.920 --> 00:29:52.000
That was a good game.

00:29:52.480 --> 00:30:25.040
Nah. Let's, um, let's fix this mess.

00:30:25.560 --> 00:30:27.960
Would you guys join me in fixing this mess?

00:30:27.960 --> 00:30:34.780
Let's, let's, let's think about what we would want in this game to make Super Pitfall a game that you would actually play.

00:30:34.980 --> 00:30:44.680
Because I think this is a game that is so bad in terms of how it actually controls and in terms of, like, what they, what they chose to include.

00:30:44.680 --> 00:30:50.500
That if we think about what is possible in the realm of the NES, I think I can do this.

00:30:50.620 --> 00:30:51.700
I thought this one through.

00:30:52.000 --> 00:30:53.380
And so here's what I have, okay?

00:30:54.160 --> 00:30:58.240
No traps that you can't see on screen beforehand.

00:30:58.240 --> 00:31:04.400
So there's, like, a, a warning or a cue that something's gonna fall apart or that.

00:31:04.720 --> 00:31:06.480
A rumble. Yeah, a rumble or something.

00:31:06.680 --> 00:31:14.280
Or that, like, a ladder leads to, like, a pit, you know, so you can at least go down there and then be like, I don't really want to fall into that and climb back up.

00:31:14.780 --> 00:31:20.720
Things that don't necessarily, like, auto-kill you for a mistake that you wouldn't have made had you have known more information.

00:31:20.720 --> 00:31:26.180
Because if you think about it, if you're exploring a cave, there's nothing stopping a guy on a ladder from looking down and saying,

00:31:26.280 --> 00:31:28.180
oh, that's a pit, and then going back up.

00:31:28.480 --> 00:31:29.880
Because we, the player, can't see that.

00:31:29.940 --> 00:31:31.540
I don't think it's fair that our character dies.

00:31:32.600 --> 00:31:41.840
Next, I don't think there should be a giant map, but I think that there should have been maps found throughout the game that lead you to the next area you need to go to.

00:31:41.960 --> 00:31:50.340
So there's a clear sense of direction that, you know, okay, cool, I've completed, you know, like, the upper right portion of the screen,

00:31:50.340 --> 00:31:55.480
and now I need to move, you know, like, just kind of like, here's where you've been, here's where you need to go next.

00:31:55.880 --> 00:31:56.720
Something like that.

00:31:57.820 --> 00:32:03.800
I would have also liked an above-ground area that you need to deliver things found in the cave.

00:32:04.060 --> 00:32:07.400
So, obviously, there would be more here than just your niece, the diamond, and...

00:32:07.400 --> 00:32:09.280
You want to introduce more backtracking?

00:32:09.480 --> 00:32:11.660
And the pet, but yeah, well, here's the reason why.

00:32:11.820 --> 00:32:15.940
It would have made me become more familiar with the layout of the cave,

00:32:15.940 --> 00:32:20.720
rather than thinking, like, that the cave is just, I don't know where I am compared to where I'm going.

00:32:20.780 --> 00:32:25.740
You'd have to learn the routes between, like, if there's something in the top right of the game,

00:32:25.760 --> 00:32:31.940
you'd have to figure out, okay, now how do I get back to the main starting point to deliver and drop off these things?

00:32:31.980 --> 00:32:37.120
I'm not saying there would be, like, a marketplace where you actually, like, barter and sell things,

00:32:37.240 --> 00:32:39.080
but just almost like...

00:32:39.080 --> 00:32:40.640
A home base. Yeah, a home base.

00:32:40.780 --> 00:32:44.640
You know what's funny? What you're describing sounds so much like SteamWorld Dig.

00:32:44.640 --> 00:32:46.060
Yeah, this is SteamWorld Dig right now.

00:32:46.080 --> 00:32:47.000
Have you played that game?

00:32:47.060 --> 00:32:48.360
I've played SteamWorld Dig, yes.

00:32:48.660 --> 00:32:50.000
But they have marketplaces.

00:32:50.160 --> 00:32:51.180
That's funny. Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:32:51.300 --> 00:32:52.380
Okay, no. No marketplace.

00:32:52.700 --> 00:32:57.140
Just, like, I'm thinking more like the Game & Watch octopus game.

00:32:57.320 --> 00:33:00.720
Yeah. Where, like, Mario goes down and he can loot the treasure.

00:33:01.140 --> 00:33:05.300
It's not Mario. It's Game & Watch in that one, but I'm thinking of the Game & Watch gallery for Game Boy.

00:33:05.460 --> 00:33:07.680
But you loot the treasure for as much as you'd like,

00:33:07.740 --> 00:33:10.760
but then your character gets heavier and smaller as you come back up.

00:33:10.760 --> 00:33:13.600
And then you just drop off all the coins that you've collected.

00:33:13.860 --> 00:33:17.860
Otherwise, if you get caught by the octopus, you lose everything.

00:33:18.060 --> 00:33:18.960
So what are your other...

00:33:18.960 --> 00:33:20.120
Do you have any more, like, big points?

00:33:20.320 --> 00:33:25.240
The other thing I was thinking was more booby traps, not cheap deaths.

00:33:25.520 --> 00:33:29.380
Think more, like, Indiana Jones-style booby traps in the cave.

00:33:29.920 --> 00:33:32.360
They can shamelessly take, like, a rolling rock.

00:33:32.480 --> 00:33:33.700
I would have liked that.

00:33:33.700 --> 00:33:37.280
That exists in sort of the Moe I had.

00:33:37.680 --> 00:33:38.700
Which is in every game.

00:33:39.960 --> 00:33:41.360
We need to talk about the Moe I had.

00:33:41.480 --> 00:33:43.240
Every game should have a Moe I had, like, section.

00:33:43.240 --> 00:33:44.460
I didn't want to talk about the Moe I had.

00:33:44.680 --> 00:33:46.620
It scared you? I'm scared of the Moe I had now.

00:33:46.740 --> 00:33:50.140
Well, this one is rather, like, large and...

00:33:50.140 --> 00:33:53.280
Imposing. Imposing compared to the other Moe I had we've faced.

00:33:53.820 --> 00:33:57.160
But other than the Moe I had, they also have, you know,

00:33:58.200 --> 00:34:01.200
the stereotypical action movie Vice Room,

00:34:01.400 --> 00:34:03.520
where things just sort of try and crush you.

00:34:03.520 --> 00:34:05.720
Yes, which is also in, like, Castlevania.

00:34:05.960 --> 00:34:07.960
Yeah. So, I mean, they do exist.

00:34:07.960 --> 00:34:09.980
They're just not very well executed.

00:34:11.060 --> 00:34:12.580
Which is, yeah, just down to, again,

00:34:12.660 --> 00:34:15.160
the poor programming of everything in the game.

00:34:15.580 --> 00:34:17.780
I do think, though, that with your changes,

00:34:17.780 --> 00:34:23.400
you would also have to change several different core concepts

00:34:23.400 --> 00:34:26.020
that govern a lot of these early NES games,

00:34:26.040 --> 00:34:32.260
like the idea of one-hit deaths and limited lives.

00:34:32.260 --> 00:34:34.300
Because if you're going to be doing...

00:34:34.300 --> 00:34:38.860
I feel like the mode of exploration that the designers,

00:34:39.240 --> 00:34:43.800
in quotes, of this game were expecting you to do

00:34:43.800 --> 00:34:47.640
was you learn the beginning by dying over and over,

00:34:47.700 --> 00:34:49.180
and you have to go through it over and over.

00:34:49.360 --> 00:34:52.240
When you introduce, well, you have to go back anyway

00:34:53.300 --> 00:34:55.140
to deliver your goods.

00:34:55.140 --> 00:35:00.000
I think that if you have both the limited amount of lives

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:02.080
and the, I guess, like, restart,

00:35:03.460 --> 00:35:05.200
the amount of times that you have to restart

00:35:05.200 --> 00:35:06.200
and start from the beginning anyway,

00:35:06.600 --> 00:35:10.020
I think that adding more backtracking will be annoying.

00:35:10.280 --> 00:35:12.680
But if you have, like, maybe a health bar

00:35:12.680 --> 00:35:14.900
and unlimited continues,

00:35:15.240 --> 00:35:16.480
then maybe, yeah, that would work.

00:35:16.680 --> 00:35:18.880
To be fair, I completely stand by

00:35:18.880 --> 00:35:21.100
that every NES game should lose lives

00:35:21.100 --> 00:35:23.940
and have a health bar instead of a one-hit death.

00:35:24.100 --> 00:35:26.600
However, in this game, I'm cool with a one-hit death

00:35:26.600 --> 00:35:28.640
because, like, you're just some random dude

00:35:28.640 --> 00:35:29.760
just down in a cave.

00:35:30.300 --> 00:35:31.160
Scorpion stings you.

00:35:31.340 --> 00:35:32.900
You're dead. Is there still a gun?

00:35:33.640 --> 00:35:34.860
There's still a gun, yes.

00:35:34.860 --> 00:35:37.980
And it works. It kills all enemies in my version of the game.

00:35:38.200 --> 00:35:40.320
I think that there's a precedent for a health bar, though.

00:35:40.460 --> 00:35:42.580
Because in the very first Pitfall,

00:35:42.820 --> 00:35:45.300
that's how... It's not a health bar, but it's, like, a health number.

00:35:45.580 --> 00:35:47.520
Yeah, yeah. You get, like, three, I think.

00:35:48.300 --> 00:35:49.960
Three? Before you're, like...

00:35:49.960 --> 00:35:52.800
They're basically lives. Right, but when you, like, hit the ground too hard,

00:35:52.960 --> 00:35:54.120
your number goes down as well.

00:35:54.200 --> 00:35:56.440
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah. I didn't even connect that.

00:35:56.640 --> 00:35:58.280
Yeah. I didn't really know what it did.

00:35:58.280 --> 00:35:59.320
I thought it was just my score.

00:35:59.780 --> 00:36:00.940
Oh, I assumed that was health.

00:36:01.080 --> 00:36:02.000
Maybe I was wrong. Yeah.

00:36:02.200 --> 00:36:04.060
But, I don't know.

00:36:04.100 --> 00:36:05.200
I think a health bar...

00:36:05.680 --> 00:36:06.740
I agree. Yeah.

00:36:06.760 --> 00:36:08.540
That's what I gotta say. I agree.

00:36:08.740 --> 00:36:10.660
Yeah, no, I would like a health bar in every NES game,

00:36:10.680 --> 00:36:13.420
and as you guys know, sometimes I try to, like, track down ROM hacks

00:36:13.420 --> 00:36:15.460
that have fixed this in games.

00:36:16.740 --> 00:36:17.860
And, lo and behold,

00:36:18.540 --> 00:36:21.540
there is a Super Pitfall ROM hack

00:36:21.540 --> 00:36:24.080
that goes above and beyond

00:36:24.080 --> 00:36:27.540
any ROM hack I've seen for an NES game so far.

00:36:27.620 --> 00:36:28.860
Is this the one that was just released?

00:36:29.100 --> 00:36:30.880
It was released pretty recently.

00:36:31.200 --> 00:36:32.960
Let me check the date for you on this.

00:36:32.960 --> 00:36:35.260
Because it's also, like, a remastered version, right?

00:36:35.260 --> 00:36:38.760
It was September 5th, 2016.

00:36:39.180 --> 00:36:42.220
Okay. But, this is the remastered version.

00:36:42.220 --> 00:36:44.340
It does work on a regular NES.

00:36:44.340 --> 00:36:48.540
If you have, like, a flash cartridge

00:36:48.540 --> 00:36:49.820
that can work on a regular NES

00:36:49.820 --> 00:36:51.480
and you plug with this ROM hack in,

00:36:51.640 --> 00:36:53.440
it will play properly on original hardware.

00:36:53.760 --> 00:36:55.260
The crazy thing is,

00:36:55.900 --> 00:36:58.760
it redesigns almost everything about this game.

00:36:58.820 --> 00:37:01.360
It's called Super Pitfall 30th Anniversary Edition.

00:37:01.360 --> 00:37:04.700
This is what I'm talking about. And it's by, it's a hack by NES Rocks.

00:37:05.200 --> 00:37:06.880
I thought he would be known for more

00:37:06.880 --> 00:37:09.120
because this is such an amazing ROM hack,

00:37:09.340 --> 00:37:12.020
but he's just known as the Super Pitfall guy.

00:37:12.020 --> 00:37:13.220
It looks pretty great, too.

00:37:13.380 --> 00:37:15.720
I played it. And it is fantastic.

00:37:16.000 --> 00:37:17.580
It's got completely new graphics,

00:37:17.980 --> 00:37:19.000
a new soundtrack,

00:37:19.500 --> 00:37:21.480
a new menu that's more colorful

00:37:21.480 --> 00:37:22.860
and plays, like, you know,

00:37:22.940 --> 00:37:24.300
like, looks more like Pitfall

00:37:24.300 --> 00:37:26.340
and shows the pyramids right off the bat

00:37:26.340 --> 00:37:28.480
so there's no, like, confusion about that.

00:37:29.380 --> 00:37:31.360
When they say that there's improved performance,

00:37:31.520 --> 00:37:33.420
they mean it because even the jump is fixed

00:37:33.420 --> 00:37:34.880
and you can move

00:37:34.880 --> 00:37:37.320
while you're falling down mid-momentum.

00:37:38.260 --> 00:37:41.020
That's cute. The only thing that was kind of weird

00:37:41.020 --> 00:37:42.200
with Super Pitfall

00:37:42.200 --> 00:37:43.560
was that the gun,

00:37:44.380 --> 00:37:46.360
even though it still exists and stuff like that,

00:37:46.440 --> 00:37:47.820
it doesn't always seem to trigger

00:37:47.820 --> 00:37:48.680
when you want it to.

00:37:49.020 --> 00:37:50.380
So that was maybe just like a...

00:37:50.380 --> 00:37:52.280
That's just keeping with the Super Pitfall heritage, though.

00:37:52.440 --> 00:37:55.200
Yeah, yeah. But there's no more hidden items.

00:37:55.540 --> 00:37:56.900
Warps are now doors

00:37:56.900 --> 00:37:58.180
instead of just, like,

00:37:58.260 --> 00:37:59.220
things you run into.

00:38:00.460 --> 00:38:02.480
There's a new HUD inside the game

00:38:02.480 --> 00:38:03.940
that explains more things to you.

00:38:04.820 --> 00:38:06.220
There are little, like,

00:38:06.260 --> 00:38:07.180
level design adjustments

00:38:07.180 --> 00:38:08.880
to make sure that the very first ladder

00:38:08.880 --> 00:38:11.200
doesn't lead to a pit of death.

00:38:11.560 --> 00:38:12.760
Like, that's nice.

00:38:13.320 --> 00:38:14.700
And if you can believe it,

00:38:14.760 --> 00:38:15.620
it's also...

00:38:16.820 --> 00:38:19.040
It's available in English and Portuguese.

00:38:19.640 --> 00:38:21.200
So it's not even just a one...

00:38:21.200 --> 00:38:22.100
I've always been looking for

00:38:22.100 --> 00:38:23.660
that Portuguese experience.

00:38:23.840 --> 00:38:26.960
Right, right. And the last thing,

00:38:27.200 --> 00:38:28.360
a seamless,

00:38:28.720 --> 00:38:30.580
fully automatic save feature.

00:38:30.860 --> 00:38:32.500
You just hold reset

00:38:32.500 --> 00:38:33.620
while shutting down

00:38:33.620 --> 00:38:37.180
and it will avoid save file corruption.

00:38:37.660 --> 00:38:38.820
That's fun. Wow.

00:38:39.060 --> 00:38:41.060
Good job, NES Rocks.

00:38:41.240 --> 00:38:43.040
Crazy. I love it.

00:38:43.580 --> 00:38:45.140
I also hope,

00:38:45.360 --> 00:38:46.400
because I need to go back

00:38:46.400 --> 00:38:49.320
to more bugs, that they fixed

00:38:49.320 --> 00:38:50.920
this particular issue.

00:38:50.920 --> 00:38:52.100
that they... I think there's...

00:38:52.100 --> 00:38:53.620
I think they found a bug,

00:38:53.920 --> 00:38:55.360
decided they didn't want to fix it,

00:38:55.460 --> 00:38:56.460
and then just made it canon.

00:38:57.360 --> 00:38:58.920
But there is...

00:38:58.920 --> 00:39:00.320
Like, you notice that

00:39:00.320 --> 00:39:01.940
you'll just fall off ladders, right?

00:39:02.420 --> 00:39:03.660
Yeah. I've noticed.

00:39:03.880 --> 00:39:05.660
I don't think that that was designed.

00:39:05.780 --> 00:39:06.960
I think that that was

00:39:06.960 --> 00:39:08.700
a problem that they did not fix.

00:39:08.840 --> 00:39:10.020
But it is in the manual.

00:39:10.180 --> 00:39:11.420
It is in the manual. We were like,

00:39:11.560 --> 00:39:12.500
let's just make it look

00:39:12.500 --> 00:39:13.500
like we planned it.

00:39:13.500 --> 00:39:14.500
So they have to fix that,

00:39:14.540 --> 00:39:16.980
but also, if there are...

00:39:16.980 --> 00:39:18.440
This is another thing that I learned from

00:39:18.440 --> 00:39:19.600
the speedrun.

00:39:19.940 --> 00:39:21.920
If you are in a screen

00:39:21.920 --> 00:39:23.660
where there are any moving...

00:39:23.660 --> 00:39:25.440
any moving sprites at all,

00:39:25.500 --> 00:39:27.240
whether it's an enemy

00:39:27.240 --> 00:39:28.360
or a moving platform

00:39:28.360 --> 00:39:29.680
or something in the background,

00:39:29.980 --> 00:39:32.340
you can just phase through walls

00:39:32.340 --> 00:39:33.800
if you walk in that direction

00:39:33.800 --> 00:39:34.700
for long enough.

00:39:35.120 --> 00:39:36.580
And it's just...

00:39:36.580 --> 00:39:37.900
All these bugs means

00:39:37.900 --> 00:39:38.720
that this game

00:39:38.720 --> 00:39:41.280
wasn't even play-tested,

00:39:41.400 --> 00:39:43.140
I feel. But Super Pitfall

00:39:43.140 --> 00:39:44.700
30th Anniversary Edition

00:39:44.700 --> 00:39:47.060
proves that this is all possible.

00:39:47.400 --> 00:39:48.800
Like, remember when you were talking earlier about the...

00:39:48.800 --> 00:39:49.780
I didn't want to spoil it,

00:39:49.800 --> 00:39:51.220
but when you were talking about the ropes

00:39:51.220 --> 00:39:52.560
and how they were kind of

00:39:52.560 --> 00:39:53.640
like glitching in and out,

00:39:54.120 --> 00:39:55.020
that's just like...

00:39:55.020 --> 00:39:56.240
That's just because they didn't know

00:39:56.240 --> 00:39:57.500
how to code this game properly.

00:39:57.900 --> 00:39:58.840
Exactly, yeah. You know, granted,

00:39:58.840 --> 00:40:00.240
this is in 2016

